{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3151","artifact_type":"feature-context","name":"plan/feature-context-sam-task-file-language.md@sha256:ac9b31164109c18a915f1fb38a8a0542fd320bb4ecaa77352ead800d82cea174"},"owner_reference":"3151","content":"# ARTIFACT:DISCOVERY\n\n## Feature\n\nRemove file-based SAM-task language from the domain model and required reading\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nA SAM task is a backend record addressed as `P{id}/T{id}`, never a file \u2014 except inside the\nlocal-YAML backend, where file storage is genuinely correct. The shared domain model\n(`sam_schema/core/models.py`) nonetheless declares a required `task_file_path` field for every\ntask in every backend, and `AGENTS.md`'s Required Reading routes every agent to\n`docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`. Because these two sources are structural/authoritative rather than\nprose, repeated prose-only corrections over ~6 months have not held: the memory and GitHub (and,\nper this session's own check, beads) backends fabricate a meaningless path just to satisfy the\nmodel, and any agent reading `AGENTS.md` or the model is correct \u2014 in good faith \u2014 to keep\nteaching the file model downstream. This item's own Root Cause analysis (issue #3151 comments)\nalready establishes this chain in detail.\n\nNote: the sibling problem on the SAM *plan* side (swarm-task-planner's file-authoring model,\n`.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md`) was already fixed by merged PRs #3159, #3161,\n#3137, #3156 \u2014 confirmed via `git log`/`gh pr list` during this session. This discovery scopes\nonly the *task*-side fix that remains open.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. No backend other than the local-YAML backend constructs, resolves, or defaults a\n   `task_file_path` (or equivalent) value to satisfy the shared task model.\n2. Any consumer currently reading `task_file_path` for task identity reads the task's address\n   (`P{id}/T{id}`) instead \u2014 including the `/dh:start-task` session-context payload and its\n   readers (`task_status_hook.py`, `implementation_manager.py`).\n3. `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` and its layer-0 duplicate are retired, and `AGENTS.md` no longer\n   routes agents to them as required reading.\n4. Remaining agent-facing prose describing SAM tasks as files (outside the local-YAML backend's\n   own docs) is swept, once nothing structural regenerates it.\n5. A test generalizes the existing single-module assertion in\n   `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` to cover every non-file backend.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n\n1. Not touching the local-YAML backend's own genuinely file-based internals\n   (`local_context_backend.py`, `writers/yaml_writer.py`, `readers/*`, their tests) \u2014 that\n   vocabulary is correct there.\n2. Not redoing the plan-side sweep already completed in #3159/#3161/#3137/#3156.\n3. Not removing file storage as a valid backend option \u2014 only removing the model's assumption\n   that *every* backend has one.\n4. Not touching legitimate legacy-format migration code/tests (`migrate_tasks_to_github.py`,\n   `test_cli_migrate_fallback.py`, `nonstandard_frontmatter_tasks.md`) \u2014 those read the old\n   format by design.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n1. Every task-bearing backend (local-YAML, memory, GitHub, beads) identifies a task by address\n   only; no backend other than local-YAML exposes or synthesizes a file path for a task.\n2. The `/dh:start-task` session-context JSON key(s) identify the task by address, not by a\n   filesystem path.\n3. `sam_schema/core/query.py`'s protocol-layer reasoning does not assume directory/file layout\n   for tasks in general (only where genuinely operating on the local-YAML backend).\n4. Agent/skill markdown outside the local-YAML backend's own documentation contains no\n   file-based task read/write instructions after the sweep.\n\n### Non-Functional\n\n1. Local-YAML backend test suites (`tests_sam/test_yaml_writer.py`, `test_detect.py`,\n   `test_yaml_reader.py`, `test_frontmatter_reader.py`, etc.) continue to pass unchanged.\n2. Memory, GitHub, and beads backend test suites continue to pass with no `task_file_path`\n   fabrication in their fixtures/assertions (existing fixtures referencing it are updated as\n   part of this work, not left stale).\n3. No consumer regresses to reading a stale/undefined field once `task_file_path` is removed\n   or relocated \u2014 this must fail loudly (type error / missing field) rather than silently, for\n   any code path not yet updated.\n\n## Design Questions for Planning\n\n<!-- HOW content from the issue's own root-cause analysis and this session's fact-check,\n     routed here rather than into Requirements. -->\n\n1. Issue author proposed a structural-first fix order: (a) remove/relocate `task_file_path`\n   from the shared model and delete the fabricating helpers in the memory and GitHub backends,\n   (b) retire `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` + its `AGENTS.md` required-reading entry + the layer-0\n   duplicate, (c) only then sweep remaining prose. Evaluate whether this exact ordering (as\n   sequential implementation tasks) is right, or whether (a) and (b) can run in parallel with\n   (c) gated behind both.\n2. Whether to delete `task_file_path` from the shared `models.py` Task type entirely, or keep it\n   as a field scoped to a local-YAML-specific subtype/protocol extension \u2014 evaluate cleanest\n   type-design approach (Optional field vs. Protocol/subclass split) given the existing\n   `TaskBackend` protocol.\n3. Whether `core/query.py`'s file/directory-layout reasoning at the protocol layer (flagged in\n   the issue's Root Cause comment) needs restructuring as part of this work, or is genuinely\n   confined to the local-YAML backend already and just needs verification.\n4. This session's own repo scan found `sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py` also defines and uses\n   `_resolve_task_file_path` (lines 1306, 1378) to fabricate a path \u2014 the original issue body\n   named only the memory and GitHub backends. Confirm beads.py needs the identical fix.\n\n## References\n\n- Issue #3151 (this item) \u2014 Root Cause and Impact Radius comments contain the full structural\n  analysis (`sam_schema/core/models.py:749`, `memory_context_backend.py:59`,\n  `github_context_backend.py:181,350`, `local_context_backend.py:72,128`)\n- This session's repo scan additionally found `beads.py:1306,1378` doing the same thing\n- `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`,\n  `AGENTS.md` lines 115 and 409 (required-reading references)\n- `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` \u2014 existing precedent assertion for one\n  module, to be generalized\n- Merged PRs that already fixed the sibling plan-side problem: #3159, #3161, #3137, #3156\n- Related agent-facing description/body contradictions already fixed: #3261 (fbe294434,\n  25fcc9564) \u2014 closed the dh-context-gathering/context-refinement side of this same drift\n- Adjacent open items in the same theme, not superseded by this work: #3141\n\n## Resolved Questions\n\n| Question | Answer | Source |\n|----------|--------|--------|\n| Is the plan-side (SAM plans, not tasks) portion of this issue already fixed? | Yes \u2014 PRs #3159, #3161, #3137, #3156 replaced the plan-file authoring model and rescoped the write-strategy rule to be mechanism-based, not agent-name-based. | `git log --grep`, `gh pr list --search` |\n| Does the task-side structural fix (task_file_path in models.py, TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md, AGENTS.md required reading) still exist unfixed? | Yes, unchanged as of this session. | `grep` of current tree |\n| Is beads.py also fabricating a task_file_path, beyond what the issue named? | Yes \u2014 `_resolve_task_file_path` at beads.py:1306/1378. | `grep` of current tree |\n| How many \"task file\" occurrences remain in agent-facing prose right now? | 57 (case-insensitive, across `.md`/`.py` in `plugins/development-harness`), down from the issue's original 138 \u2014 the plan-side sweep already landed. | `grep -rli` count this session |\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- None blocking. All Design Questions above are routed to planning research, not human\n  escalation \u2014 the issue's own analysis plus this session's verification resolve WHO/WHAT/WHY\n  without unbound constraints, domain-knowledge gaps, or contradictory requirements.\n\n## User Confirmation\n\n- [x] User confirms this document captures their intent (self-initialized from a thoroughly\n  pre-analyzed backlog item; user said \"ready you may start\" after confirming no other issue\n  should land first \u2014 treated as confirmation per the AutoMode branch of the Human Touchpoint\n  Gate)\n"}